## kosh vendors nothing and links nothing

It drives the CHCE engines across a process boundary, so no engine code is
compiled into it and no engine licence reaches it. There is no `vendor/`
directory and nothing under `kosh/` is copied from another project.

## Runtime dependencies

Nine packages are imported at runtime. Their licences are their own; the table
below was read from each installed package's metadata
(`importlib.metadata`), not from a project page.

| Package | Licence |
|---|---|
| `typer` | MIT |
| `rich` | MIT |
| `zstandard` | BSD-3-Clause |
| `brotli` | MIT |
| `zopfli` | Apache-2.0 |
| `numpy` | BSD-3-Clause AND 0BSD AND MIT AND Zlib AND CC0-1.0 |
| `fastapi` | MIT |
| `uvicorn` | BSD-3-Clause |
| `python-multipart` | Apache-2.0 |

Versions are pinned by range in `pyproject.toml`, so the exact set installed
depends on the environment; the licences above are stable across the versions in
use, and each package ships its own `LICENSE` in the installed distribution —
that copy, not this table, is the authority.

Nothing in kosh phones home: the UI server binds to localhost, and the only
network use in the repository is in development scripts that fetch test corpora.

## Development-only dependencies

`pytest`, `pillow`, `httpx2` and `hypothesis` are in the `dev` extra. They are not
imported by `kosh/` at runtime and do not ship in the package. `httpx2` is listed
because starlette's `TestClient` imports it; nothing in `kosh/` imports it.

